    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-29fcb9f8e9fb\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"nwc-response-missing-e-tag-ts\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\b23195\\\\b.*\\\\btags[\\\"']?\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*[\\\"']p[\\\"']\\\\s*,[^\\\\[\\\\]]*\\\\]\\\\s*\\\\]|\\\\btags[\\\"']?\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*[\\\"']p[\\\"']\\\\s*,[^\\\\[\\\\]]*\\\\]\\\\s*\\\\].*\\\\b23195\\\\b\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.ts\"},{\"id\":\"nwc-response-missing-e-tag-js\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\b23195\\\\b.*\\\\btags[\\\"']?\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*[\\\"']p[\\\"']\\\\s*,[^\\\\[\\\\]]*\\\\]\\\\s*\\\\]|\\\\btags[\\\"']?\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*[\\\"']p[\\\"']\\\\s*,[^\\\\[\\\\]]*\\\\]\\\\s*\\\\].*\\\\b23195\\\\b\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.js\"},{\"id\":\"nwc-response-missing-e-tag-py\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\b23195\\\\b.*\\\\btags[\\\"']?\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*[\\\"']p[\\\"']\\\\s*,[^\\\\[\\\\]]*\\\\]\\\\s*\\\\]|\\\\btags[\\\"']?\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*[\\\"']p[\\\"']\\\\s*,[^\\\\[\\\\]]*\\\\]\\\\s*\\\\].*\\\\b23195\\\\b\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.py\"}],\"coverage\":\"Flagrant one-line case only: an added line in a .ts, .js or .py file that builds an NWC response event (kind 23195) whose literal tags array holds just a single p tag, so the e tag is missing.\",\"residual\":\"Does the hunk build or dispatch NWC messages in a way that leaves out the response's e tag (other than a one-line literal kind-23195 event whose tags are only a p tag), p-tags the wrong party (a request not tagged with the wallet service, or a response not tagged with the client), or executes a request whose expiration timestamp has already passed?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/nwc/respond.ts b/src/nwc/respond.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/nwc/respond.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+const ev = { kind: 23195, tags: [[\\\"p\\\", clientPubkey]], content: enc };\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/lib/nwc.js b/lib/nwc.js\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/lib/nwc.js\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+const ev = { kind: 23195, tags: [[\\\"p\\\", clientPubkey]], content: enc };\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/nwc/respond.py b/nwc/respond.py\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/nwc/respond.py\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+event = {\\\"kind\\\": 23195, \\\"tags\\\": [[\\\"p\\\", client_pubkey]], \\\"content\\\": enc}\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/nwc/respond.ts b/src/nwc/respond.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/nwc/respond.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+const ev = { kind: 23195, tags: [[\\\"p\\\", clientPubkey], [\\\"e\\\", requestId]], content: enc };\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"Literal response events (kind 23195) whose single-line tags array holds only a p tag can be checked mechanically. To spot a wrong p-tag recipient, the checker would need to know which variable holds whose pubkey. Expiration handling is control-flow logic. Tags spread over several lines or added later also need judgement. Constraints cover only the .ts, .js and .py extensions.\"}",
